445 0 obj
<<
/A 1883 0 R
/Alt (Three-panel flowchart on flood resilience. Panel a: Flood Resilience Index Construction. Data collection includes POI, Population, Road network, Precipitation, NPP, DEM, Night light, NDVI, Landuse, GDP. Data preprocessing involves Network, Hydrological, Raster, Regional tabulation, Kernel density, Spatial interpolation, Buffer analysis. Multidimensional Assessment \(R-R-A Framework\) covers Resistance, Recoverability, Adaptability with sub-indicators. Index evaluation system lists Socio Economic, Urban Development Index, Emergency Rescue, Medical Facility POI Density, Logistics, Transportation Facility POI Density. Panel b: Data Processing and Machine Learning Model Comparison. Standardized indicator values flow from Original data to Log/Box-Cox transformation, then Min-max normalization. Indicator weight determined by EWM and CRITIC Method, leading to W formula, Grid flood resilience score, and Normally distributed grid data \(FR grid formula\). Model performance evaluation metrics: R squared, RMSE/MAE, AUC. Models compared: OLS, RF, LightGBM, XGBoost \(best model\). Panel c: Attribution analysis of Flood Resilience differences using XGBoost-SHAP. Indicators affecting FR: Rainfall Intensity RI, Population Density PD, Grey Infrastructure Index L_GRI, Landscape Diversity Index SHDI, Public Service Density PSD, Topographic Wetness Index TWI.)
/K 13
/P 37 0 R
/Pg 14 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
