/Alt (The four-panel graph, arranged in two rows of two, shows SHAP values for influencing factors across four years: 2012, 2016, 2020, and 2023. Each panel contains a horizontal bar graph on the left and a scatter plot on the right. The horizontal axis for the bar graphs is labeled Mean SHAP value, ranging from 0.00 to 0.02. The horizontal axis for the scatter plots is labeled SHAP value, ranging from 0.0 to 0.3. The vertical axis for both is labeled with factors: TWI, PSD, RI, SHDI, PD, DI, and L GRI. A vertical color bar on the far right of each panel indicates Feature value from Low to High. Each panel also includes a pie chart showing percentage contributions for some factors. In panel a, 2012, TWI has the highest mean SHAP value at 0.0220. In panel b, 2016, TWI again has the highest mean SHAP value at 0.0238. In panel c, 2020, TWI is highest at 0.0212. In panel d, 2023, TWI is highest at 0.0213. Across all panels, TWI consistently shows the highest mean SHAP value, while L GRI and DI consistently show the lowest mean SHAP values. The scatter plots show the distribution of SHAP values for each factor, with higher feature values generally corresponding to higher SHAP values for TWI, PSD, and RI.)
