877 0 obj
<<
/A 2094 0 R
/Alt (The eight-panel map, arranged in two rows of four, displays spatial patterns of SHAP factors and their contribution magnitudes across a geographic region. Each panel shows a map of the same region with varying SHAP values indicated by a gradient scale. Panel a, labeled SHDI, shows SHAP values ranging from minus 0.019 to 0.031. Panel b, labeled RI, shows SHAP values from minus 0.019 to 0.044. Panel c, labeled TWI, shows SHAP values from minus 0.031 to 0.079. Panel d, labeled L_GRI, shows SHAP values from minus 0.02 to 0.021. Panel e, labeled PSD, shows SHAP values from minus 0.011 to 0.236. Panel f, labeled DI, shows SHAP values from minus 0.012 to 0.029. Panel g, labeled PD, shows SHAP values from minus 0.014 to 0.028. Panel h, labeled Main SHAP, shows the dominant SHAP factor for each area, with a legend indicating PSD, PD, RI, SHDI, and TWI. All panels include a scale bar indicating 0 to 200 kilometers.)
/K 58
/P 37 0 R
/Pg 25 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
